ng that we had to verify  and once we knew that that was true  then we placed more importance on other  ancillary things  like capital costs cost of the assay  uh ease of use assuming a lab  tech time all those things then came  into play and they were all in favor of  represent so that's why we ultimately  made the decision  to move to their assay  great thank you now what recommendations  can you make to anyone who wants to test  the leading pgt  platforms in their own lab  uh again i would say you really want to  get your hands on it  and and try it out for yourself um  i know that can be easier said than done  depending on on your particular  situation if you don't have  the sequencing equipment in your lab  work with your local representatives  see if if demos are a possibility  if you know another lab that has the  equipment that you can run around but  really  you need to have first hand experience  to know if it's the right choice for  your lab  thank you so much and again to the  audience any questions that we did not  have time for today  will be addressed by our seekers via the  contact information that you  provided at the time of registration  so thank you so much adam and caroline  for your time today adam do you have any  final comments for  our audience before we go  no i would just like to thank you for  having me and thank everyone for  listening  thank you again adam for your time today  and for your research  we would also like to thank lab roots  and our sponsor  thermo fisher scientific for  underwriting today's  educational webcast this webcast can be  viewed on demand  and labyrinths will alert you via email  when it's available for replay  we encourage you to share that email  with your colleagues who may have missed  today's  live event until next time take care  goodbye
 

